<title>USA: Cramer sells most of Dow Jones stake.</title>
<headline>Cramer sells most of Dow Jones stake.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>James Cramer, president of Cramer Berkowitz &amp; Co, sold most of the one million shares of Dow Jones &amp; Co Inc that he controlled over the last few weeks, his office said.</p>
<p>Cramer declined to comment.</p>
<p>The hedge fund manager had tried to pressure Dow Jones to sell its electronic-information unit, Dow Jones Markets, formerly known as Telerate.</p>
<p>Dow Jones announced in January that it planned to invest as much as $650 million over the next three years to  strengthen the unit.</p>
</text>
